<title>POLAND: Poland C/A deficit up to $984 mln in Jan-Nov.</title>
<headline>Poland C/A deficit up to $984 mln in Jan-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account deficit of $125 million in November bringing the shortfall in the January-November period to $984 million, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	    NOV 96	  OCT 96    NOV 95</p>
<p> current account million USD	    -125	    -548*	-552</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	  -805	  -1,131	 -214</p>
<p> exports				 2,145	   2,196	2,081</p>
<p> imports				 2,950	   3,327	2,295</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	  525	     626	  670</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>					 JAN-NOV 1996  JAN-NOV 1995</p>
<p> current account million USD	    -984	   4,959</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-7,196	  -1,323</p>
<p> exports				21,973	  20,889</p>
<p> imports				29,169	  22,212</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	6,668	   7,089</p>
<p>Note. Figures marked * are revised. From January 1996 the central bank introduced a new category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot; which encompasses mainly cross-border, unregistered trade flows.     -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
